+## Payment-result evidence guard
+
+Install the sibling reference checker before running this app:
+
+```bash
+python -m pip install -e ../payment-result-guard
+```
+
+Promise capture now requires a supported customer statement in one completed
+attempt, in addition to the existing binding, right-party, confidence and date
+policy checks. Missing or ambiguous evidence records a review reason in the
+existing rejection event. Conditional plans are not ordinary promises, and saying
+"paid" is not proof of receipt. No new payment or reconciliation operation is added.
+
+The week1/week2 fixtures now use explicit synthetic numeric/date statements for the
+existing fixed-date demonstration. Older word-number or relative-date evidence is
+outside the guard's bounded grammar and may be reviewed. This is an intentional
+acceptance change, not a claim to understand all spoken English. Existing dispute
+handling is retained and is not certified by the promise guard.
+
+See [the shared tool](../payment-result-guard/README.md) for the offline harness and
+[validation](../../../docs/payment-result-guard/validation.md) for evidence levels.
