 ## 📄 License
 
-MIT
\ No newline at end of file
+MIT
+## Local payment-result guard
+
+The webhook now calls the shared Python evidence checker before recording a retry
+recommendation. Install `apps/python/payment-result-guard` into a Python 3.11+
+environment and set `PAYMENT_GUARD_PYTHON` to that environment's absolute interpreter
+path before starting this Node server. The bridge has a five-second timeout, no
+shell invocation and bounded JSON I/O. An absent or failed checker produces a
+reviewable unknown decision; it never enables unguarded retry advice.
+
+The existing advisory boundary and zero recovered amount remain unchanged. A
+negative/conditional/missing transcript cannot become retry consent. Evidence now
+requests an exact customer quote; older paraphrases may need review. Card-update
+requests do not receive a fabricated Billing Portal URL. Pause/update requests are
+review-only in this narrow implementation, not executed actions. Local canceled
+calls ignore late results. Existing event-registration-before-re-fetch recovery
+limitations remain; this patch does not implement a webhook transaction/outbox.
+
+```bash
+# After installing this app's dev dependencies and the sibling Python package:
+PAYMENT_GUARD_PYTHON=/absolute/path/to/venv/bin/python CALLE_API_KEY=mock npm test
+```
+
+Tests invoke the actual POST handler and shared Python process with mock provider
+lookup and mocked database boundaries. They are local runtime integration tests,
+not live CALL-E, Stripe, or database end-to-end tests. The direct SDK mock now
+includes explicit synthetic transcript turns. No real recipient is called by tests.
+Build tracing may warn about the server-configured Python executable; standalone
+packaging and remote deployment are not verified.
+
+See [the shared harness](../../python/payment-result-guard/README.md) for repeatable
+results across both applications.
