+# Validation iterations
+
+## Original implementation: 5da61d3
+
+Bounded core, kept and Recover adapters, and local host paths were verified using
+42 synthetic fixtures and 302 tests (58 core, 195 kept, 49 Recover). These are
+historical local results, not live customer or production outcomes.
+
+## Telephone observation rounds
+
+1. Browser planning: preparation was interrupted; no live call evidence obtained.
+2. First API call: about 8.84 seconds, greeting only; no commitment sample.
+3. Default-receiver restart: P01 about 67 seconds, P02 about 46.4 seconds; receiver
+   declined payment commitment/approval role-play. P03 was not placed in that round.
+4. Scripted system-test wording: receiver consented to fictional line reading.
+   P01 (59 seconds) returned an incomplete invoice phrase instead of the target.
+   P02 (49.6 seconds) retained "If approved" but transcript and extraction contained
+   100100 instead of the intended 100.00. P03 (45.1 seconds) returned the complete
+   denial line. Audio origin of the amount discrepancy remains unverified.
+
+These are author-observed real AI-to-AI test calls, not real customers or debt.
+The contributed samples preserve the fictional utterances and extraction values,
+replace call identifiers, and omit account data, phone numbers, timestamps,
+recordings and credentials. Raw records remain private. This repository only
+replays these sanitized samples offline; it does not independently verify a
+provider's past execution, rerun extraction, or validate host writes.
+
+## Replay supplement (delivery v0.2)
+
+Problem: provider task completion and passing guard regressions could be mistaken
+for successful target acquisition. All three scripted calls had task_completed
+true, although only P03 yielded the exact target line.
+
+Change: add independent acquisition diagnostics and a coverage-sensitive CLI mode,
+three sanitized replay fixtures, five regression checks, and integration into the
+existing verification harness. The financial core and both adapters are unchanged.
+Regression match and target coverage are separate output fields and exit policies.
+The default replay succeeds for the observed behavior; `--require-targets` fails
+until every target is obtained. It must not be made green by rewriting transcripts.
+
+Validation sequence: new tests initially failed because the replay module did not
+exist; implementation then passed all 63 core tests. Full harness outputs accompany
+the delivery. No new live calls were made for this supplement.
+
+Limit: unclear/refused outcomes return unsupported before deeper evidence checks.
+These replays do not establish independent condition or amount detection by the
+core, nor a benefit over kept's existing refusal of those outcomes. A supported
+rejection classification and general speech-number parsing remain outside scope.
+
+## Next experiment, not a measured improvement
+
+Keep invoice identifiers in metadata and speak only one short sample sentence
+at a time. Announce a fictional audio test and obtain consent; stop on refusal.
+For an authorized new call, clarify a mismatch at most once, preserve both original
+and corrected turns, and never silently substitute the intended amount. End after
+90 seconds; no automatic redial. Do not bypass receiver rules.
+
+P01 still needs a complete target sample. P02 needs amount/audio verification.
+Recover's live permission scenario and real host writes require separate evidence.
+These prompt adjustments have not been tested in a new live call.
